// ✅ FIXED (2026-07-14, seed rcdzc) — REGRESSION WITNESS. A plain `//` LINE COMMENT at the top
// level USED TO hide the following top-level form: the ML reader wraps a leading line comment as
// `(comment "…" <next-form>)`, and the top-level SCAN did not see through the wrapper, so the
// wrapped `def`/`type`/`export` became invisible ("unbound name `comment`" + the def's own name
// unbound). A sibling landed `strip_comments` in `Db::load` (db.rs) which peels the wrapper before
// every scan; this file — which leads with 20-odd `//` lines and has `//` between/around its forms
// — now `cdz check`s CLEAN. It is kept as the regression witness: if the peel regresses, this file
// goes red again.
//
// Placements verified fixed (all clean): a `//` (or `///`) leading ANY top-level form (def/type/
// export/@test/effect), a `//` BETWEEN two defs, a TRAILING-INLINE `//`, a `//` with a blank line
// after it, and a `//` inside a body. The one residual gap — a comment on an `(import …)` form,
// hidden from the LINK scan (which runs before `Db::load`'s strip) — was fixed the same day in
// `compile.rs::link_inputs` (see `check_imports_cli.rs::a_comment_on_an_import_is_seen_through…`).
def f(x: Int64) = x

export { f }
